<title>GERMANY: SWIMMING-WORLD RECORD FOR WOUDA IN MEN'S 400 METRES MEDLEY.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-WORLD RECORD FOR WOUDA IN MEN'S 400 METRES MEDLEY.</headline>
<dateline>GELSENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marcel Wouda of the Netherlands set a world record for the short-course men's 400 metres individual medley when he clocked four minutes 5.59 seconds at a World Cup meeting on Saturday.</p>
<p>The previous best of 4:06.03 was set by Finland's Jani Sievinen in Lappeenranta, Finland, in January 1996.</p>
